<p class="comparison-note">Prices exclude GST where the company's site states so. Ours is GST-inclusive. Ongoing hosting is separate for most providers — Ahoy Studio, for example, publishes hosting at NZ$450 + GST per year paid to Rocketspark, plus NZ$35 + GST for the domain.</p>

<h2>Who each one actually suits</h2>

<h3>Ahoy Studio</h3>
<p>A design-led studio with genuinely good-looking work, building on the Rocketspark platform. Copywriting and Google setup are included, and the price is published openly — which is rarer than it should be in this industry.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> a tradie who cares about design quality and wants a small, sharp three-page site. <strong>Worth knowing:</strong> at NZ$3,395 + GST for three pages it's the highest published per-page price here, and hosting is an additional annual cost paid to a third party.</p>

<h3>Trades Online</h3>
<p>The most complete published pricing structure of anyone in this space — three tiers, clear page counts, honest about the range. Copywriting and SEO are included across packages, and they're upfront that final pricing depends on scope.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> a tradie who wants tiers to choose between, or who needs more than five pages and expects to grow into a bigger site. <strong>Worth knowing:</strong> 4–6 weeks is a longer build than some, and the ranges are wide enough that you'll need a conversation to land on a number.</p>

<h3>Tradie Design</h3>
<p>A broader creative outfit doing website design alongside branding, print and advertising — so a good option if you want your signage, vehicle livery and website to match.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> a tradie who wants branding and website handled together by one shop. <strong>Worth knowing:</strong> nothing is published on price, turnaround or inclusions, so you'll need to ring to find out. That's a normal way to run an agency, but it does make comparison harder.</p>

<h3>WFT — us</h3>
<p>Flat {{ site.priceDisplay }}, five or more pages, live in {{ site.buildDays }}, copywriting and local SEO included, and the only enquiry guarantee we're aware of in this market: no genuine job enquiry within {{ site.guaranteeDays }} days and we rebuild it free.</p>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> a tradie who wants it done fast, at a known price, with someone carrying part of the risk. <strong>Worth knowing, honestly:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>We're new.</strong> The companies above have track records and client work you can look at. We don't yet, which is why our first ten clients get {{ site.foundingDiscountDisplay }} off in exchange for an honest review.</li>
  <li><strong>We don't do bespoke.</strong> E-commerce, booking systems, customer portals — not us. Trades Online's Advanced tier or a full agency is the right call.</li>
  <li><strong>The guarantee has conditions</strong>, including staying on our {{ site.planPriceDisplay }} plan for the 90 days. They're <a href="/guarantee/">published in full</a> rather than buried.</li>
  <li><strong>We only build for trades, in New Zealand.</strong> That's what makes the price and speed possible, and it's a real limit.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What actually separates these companies</h2>
<p>Strip out the marketing and there are four real variables:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Is copywriting included?</strong> Every specialist here includes it. General web designers frequently don't, and it's the biggest hidden cost — NZ$800–$1,500 bought separately.</li>
  <li><strong>Is local SEO setup included?</strong> Again, the specialists include it. Ask a generalist directly, and get the add-on price before comparing.</li>
  <li><strong>How fast?</strong> Between one and six weeks across this table. Whether that matters depends entirely on you.</li>
  <li><strong>Does anyone carry risk?</strong> This is the one where the market is uniformly silent. Almost nobody in New Zealand web design offers anything if the site doesn't produce work.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Questions to ask whoever you choose</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Is copywriting included, or do I write it?</li>
  <li>Is local SEO setup included, or an add-on? What does the add-on cost?</li>
  <li>Whose name is the domain registered in? <em>(It should be yours.)</em></li>
  <li>What are the ongoing costs, and who do I pay them to?</li>
  <li>What does a content change cost after launch?</li>
  <li>If I want to leave, do I get my site?</li>
  <li>What happens if it doesn't bring in any enquiries?</li>
</ul>
<p>That last one is worth asking everywhere, including us. Most answers will be some version of "nothing" — which is standard, and worth knowing before you sign rather than after.</p>

